1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,020
Cinderella

2
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:11,750
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:20,150
Cinderella's Sister

4
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,690
Your room is still being constructed

5
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:32,710
so for a few days you will be sharing my room. Come this way.

6
00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:38,410
Episode 2

7
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:44,510
Come and sit.

8
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:53,810
We have become like this.

9
00:00:53,810 --> 00:00:58,210
Did you ever imagine this would happen when we met on the train?

10
00:00:58,210 --> 00:01:01,300
Isn't it very very amazing?

11
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:07,270
I am sorry for not knowing you were my unni and not my age.

12
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:12,570
- But you look really young.
- Where can I wash?

13
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:14,990
I asked where I can shower?

14
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:18,450
Oh. There.

15
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:23,560
You need to change your clothes.

16
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,560
It's not in here.

17
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:36,930
This is for your stuff. I emptied it.

18
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:39,730
This is new. I bought it for you.

19
00:01:39,730 --> 00:01:42,440
Are you always that talkative?

20
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:44,040
How did you know?

21
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:48,430
I am very talkative.

22
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:52,180
Unni, the pajamas.

23
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:56,890
Come out and then change.

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,410
The red toothbrush is yours and the blue is mine.

25
00:02:51,010 --> 00:02:56,440
Put your hand under. When you put it under, the water comes out.

26
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:26,120
So because my mother was sick, saying the air here was good, my dad built the house here.

27
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:30,400
But the brewery was too far away to travel to

28
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:34,740
so he built the brewery right next to the house.

29
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:38,580
Since then, I've lived here.

30
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:41,440
How far did get before?

31
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:43,810
Ah, was it until I was seven?

32
00:03:43,810 --> 00:03:47,750
Then the year changed and I was eight.

33
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:53,930
- What is it?
- Your life story is boring.I don't want to hear it.

34
00:03:53,930 --> 00:03:57,610
Then, should I skip to when I was ten?

35
00:03:57,610 --> 00:04:02,530
Starting when I was ten, it got really interesting.

36
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:06,210
Unni where are you going. I'll go with you.

37
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:12,840
Not if you don't want me to.

38
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:16,190
Why so sudden?

39
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:58,180
Hey, happy to see you.

40
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:00,370
I was getting bored.

41
00:05:00,370 --> 00:05:05,410
Want to come and have a drink? When there isn't a guest, this annex is empty at night.

42
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,160
Come over here.

43
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:13,540
Is there something you want to sponge off of me?

44
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:16,180
Huh? Sponge off of you?

45
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:21,760
Why are you smiling? There's nothing you can sponge off me, so quit smiling.

46
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:25,940
Wait a sec. Theres something I have to ask you.

47
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:29,240
Do you smile when sponging off of someone?

48
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:32,880
That was the first time I heard that in my life.

49
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:39,240
It was laughable so I smiled, it was humorous so I smiled, I was joyful, so I smiled. It was nice so I smiled.

50
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:45,290
There weren't just one or two reasons to smile. Why of all things do you need to sponge off someone to smile?

51
00:05:46,810 --> 00:05:50,030
- Is it laughable now?
- Huh?

52
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:57,610
Laughable? Humorous? Nice? Joyful? Why are you smiling now?

53
00:05:57,610 --> 00:06:01,410
Am I smiling now?

54
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:09,870
She belittled me.

55
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:24,180
♫ In the colors is the rainbow that we see shining? (In Spanish}

56
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:30,220
♫ And that is why I love

57
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:36,260
♫ the great loves of many colors

58
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:23,090
Stand at attention. Bow.

59
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:25,660
Thank you.

60
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:35,260
Unni. I'm going to the store. Can if buy you anything?

61
00:07:36,410 --> 00:07:38,700
While you are on your knees ...

62
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:44,460
"yo" (being polite, sarcastically) What should I call you? Just by your name?

63
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:47,270
Or if not, "Unni"?

64
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,090
Don't call me.

65
00:07:58,910 --> 00:08:02,480
Hey, what is this? I was being nice because she is your sister.

66
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,450
What a loser.

67
00:08:04,450 --> 00:08:06,560
C'mon!

68
00:08:23,130 --> 00:08:25,890
What is he doing?

69
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:10,820
Bought a kiddie helmet...

70
00:09:14,970 --> 00:09:19,490
Scared you? "What are you doing here?" Isn't that what you are going to say?

71
00:09:19,490 --> 00:09:24,180
I mean the reason Hong Gi Tae came here ...

72
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:32,500
What's the score with the guy who shot this? Are you splitting it in half?

73
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:35,260
Or sixty- forty?

74
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:38,220
Oh. Seventy-thirty.

75
00:09:40,210 --> 00:09:43,640
With things like this, you're quite smart.

76
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,430
If you put these things in the newspaper, there will be talk.

77
00:09:46,430 --> 00:09:53,930
Chairman Hong Han Seok, your hidden youngest child Gi Hoon

78
00:09:54,000 --> 00:10:01,800
was abused by his older brothers and father.

79
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:06,360
So your youngest is doing odd jobs for a local brewery.

80
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:09,870
They are perfect grist for grinding slowly in a rumor mill.

81
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:14,670
Smart brain, very smart brain.

82
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:26,020
Why? Isn't this enough? Are you smiling?

83
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:29,300
Nice to see you, Gi Tae. It's been a long time.

84
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:35,650
Hyung Gi Tae. If you have something to say, say it. Leave out the Hyung.

85
00:10:35,650 --> 00:10:38,220
Is Hyung Gi Jeong also doing well?

86
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:41,330
You keep being a loser.

87
00:10:41,330 --> 00:10:47,860
I mean leave out all the titles attached to family relationships when you talk.

88
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:50,600
I've never taken pictures like this.

89
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:54,330
It seems some bad man who needs money caught you.

90
00:10:54,330 --> 00:10:57,640
Since you brought the pictures here, it seems you resolved the situation.

91
00:10:57,640 --> 00:11:00,610
So there isn't a problem anymore.

92
00:11:00,610 --> 00:11:03,500
Because I don't like calling you hyung,

93
00:11:06,930 --> 00:11:13,020
Hong Gi Tae. You son of a bitch. There was no reason for you to hit me.

94
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,960
You told me stay away and I am.

95
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:19,400
You said to live quietly so I live here quietly.

96
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:23,340
I was lucky to meet a good man here and I am doing well here.

97
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:28,510
Don't appear in front of me and leave me alone. Got it?

98
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:52,220
Unni! Unni, let's go together.

99
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:59,380
Mom and dad are coming back from their honeymoon today. Let's go to the airport together.

100
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:06,460
Oppa Gi Hoon said he would give us a ride. Oh, there he is. Oppa!

101
00:12:09,910 --> 00:12:13,930
Unni, hurry.

102
00:12:13,930 --> 00:12:15,710
Unni!

103
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:19,120
Let's just go.

104
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:23,130
Why? I'm going to go together with Unni.

105
00:12:23,130 --> 00:12:25,980
She's not the type who will ever listen to others.

106
00:12:54,030 --> 00:12:57,420
Elders, please this way.

107
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:46,690
This is my grandfather's brother.

108
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:11,360
My father's cousin and his wife.

109
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,910
My father's second cousin's wife.

110
00:14:55,290 --> 00:14:58,330
Please say something, aunt.

111
00:15:01,590 --> 00:15:04,060
What are the four pillars of your destiny (i.e. birth year, month, day, and time)?

112
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:09,980
Excuse me?

113
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,410
That grandma used to be a shaman...

114
00:15:14,410 --> 00:15:18,020
I mean, a spiritual person but now she is a pastor.

115
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:22,740
I guess her spirit and Jesus come to her alternately, very funny, right?

116
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:27,830
Right now, she seems to be getting intense vibes from you.

117
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:26,540
What a complicated family...

118
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:29,130
Why so many family relations and why force me to bow

119
00:16:29,130 --> 00:16:32,480
to even second cousins twice removed of in-laws?

120
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:35,540
Aigoo, what a nasty lot I have...

121
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:42,370
In a house where I came to improve my lot, even if I fall backward...

122
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:55,090
Because of my swollen feet.

123
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:13,110
Let me see your feet.

124
00:17:32,090 --> 00:17:38,510
This is a family with lots of relations, talks and incidents.

125
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:42,720
I am sorry for making your life harder.

126
00:17:56,990 --> 00:18:03,720
Under the sky there were only Eun Jo and me, the two of us.

127
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:12,610
Are you done messaging them?

128
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:23,410
I have never been someone belonging to some family.

129
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:30,640
My Eun Jo... Except for her mom, she never had a father

130
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:37,910
or someone to call uncle or aunt.

131
00:18:40,070 --> 00:18:44,500
It feels like the day when we finally

132
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:47,290
get to have a roof after living in a roofless house for a long time.

133
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:53,180
Thank you. I will do my best.

134
00:18:53,950 --> 00:18:55,830
Thank you.

135
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:04,190
If you think you're going to regret this, tell me now.

136
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:13,530
Why? What is wrong?

137
00:19:14,770 --> 00:19:21,740
People tell me that I seem ill-starred.

138
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:27,760
What use is my ravishing beauty when it will destroy my husband?

139
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:32,570
But what on earth are you talking about? Who says such nonsense?

140
00:19:32,570 --> 00:19:38,200
Why do you think your father's second cousin's wife asked about my four pillars of destiny?

141
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:42,980
It is not like that. It's a useless worry.

142
00:19:42,980 --> 00:19:47,120
She asks anybody about their four pillars.

143
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:51,360
Tell me now if you think you are going to regret this.

144
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:54,560
We haven't registered our marriage yet.

145
00:19:56,970 --> 00:19:59,910
I feel sorry that you have such thoughts.

146
00:19:59,910 --> 00:20:03,280
With me, you don't have to worry about such things.

147
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:11,900
Promise me, you will not be like this.

148
00:20:21,930 --> 00:20:24,750
This foot hurts too.

149
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:27,140
Oh, okay.

150
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:34,900
Dad, Grandma Aunt says...

151
00:20:52,930 --> 00:20:56,390
Oh! Are you okay?

152
00:21:08,830 --> 00:21:11,140
When you enter elders' rooms,

153
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:15,050
giving a sign of your entering will be a polite thing to do, right?

154
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:24,530
Oh... I've never had to do this so...

155
00:21:24,530 --> 00:21:29,220
I have no manners so...

156
00:22:59,290 --> 00:23:02,630
What are you talking about, Aunt?

157
00:23:02,630 --> 00:23:07,070
Until I say you can do it, delay the registration of the marriage.

158
00:23:08,670 --> 00:23:12,580
She's not an ordinary one. It's not her.

159
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:17,040
- Ma'am-
- If we make a mistake, it'll be disastrous.

160
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:22,700
Goodness, I don't want to imagine it. My body is just-

161
00:23:23,460 --> 00:23:27,650
It's written on her face. She'll completely take advantage of you, too.

162
00:23:27,650 --> 00:23:34,580
So delay registering the marriage until I say so. Understand?

163
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:36,160
Don't be like that, Aunt.

164
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,430
What do you mean by don't be like that?

165
00:23:37,430 --> 00:23:41,680
Whatever you don't know well and whatever you do know well, please don't say anything about either.

166
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:43,680
What do you know about that person?

167
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:47,770
That person and her daughter are now my family.

168
00:23:47,770 --> 00:23:51,660
Don't say such hollow things about my family. Stop it now.

169
00:23:51,660 --> 00:23:53,350
What do I do about what I can see with my own eyes.

170
00:23:53,350 --> 00:23:55,580
Then, don't look.

171
00:23:57,820 --> 00:24:02,160
Look here, Nephew. Look here.

172
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:04,760
They're my family now.

173
00:24:04,770 --> 00:24:09,390
Stop saying such hollow things about my family now.

174
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:13,760
Look here, Nephew!

175
00:24:26,130 --> 00:24:28,660
I was looking for you for ages.

176
00:24:37,740 --> 00:24:40,130
It's not worth trying to walk away.

177
00:24:40,130 --> 00:24:45,770
If you wait a bit, all the elders who are spending the night here like me will arrive.

178
00:24:53,130 --> 00:24:56,460
There's somewhere good to hide. Should I fill you in?

179
00:24:56,460 --> 00:24:59,240
It's nice to see everyone in the family come together.

180
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:00,190
Definitely.

181
00:25:00,190 --> 00:25:02,700
Days like today are hard to come by.

182
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:04,790
Ah, of course.

183
00:25:04,790 --> 00:25:08,140
Where is it?

184
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:17,280
Excuse me, excuse me. I've got a mom and a sister now!

185
00:25:17,280 --> 00:25:20,820
Isn't my mom really pretty?

186
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:24,600
Applause! Applause!

187
00:25:24,700 --> 00:25:27,220
Let's sit.

188
00:25:31,330 --> 00:25:34,470
Father, have some.

189
00:25:43,350 --> 00:25:47,500
Uncle! Have you not seen my Unni, Eun Joo?

190
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:49,460
I don't know.

191
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:54,360
Uncle! Then what about Gi Hoon?

192
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:56,850
I don't know!

193
00:26:08,660 --> 00:26:13,120
It's chrysanthemum. Do you want to try a sip?

194
00:26:51,570 --> 00:26:54,430
You should sit here and do it. Otherwise, you'll hurt your back.

195
00:27:36,580 --> 00:27:39,570
Has he not seen my message?

196
00:27:39,570 --> 00:27:43,650
Or, did I press the wrong number?

197
00:27:43,650 --> 00:27:48,220
Does it make sense that none of my 10 text messages were delivered?

198
00:27:49,660 --> 00:27:53,530
I think I need to change my carrier, right?

199
00:27:53,530 --> 00:27:59,860
Unni, what carrier service do you use? Do your messages ever stop sending?

200
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:03,650
If not, should I change mine to be the same as yours?

201
00:28:05,190 --> 00:28:07,350
Are you an idiot?

202
00:28:09,340 --> 00:28:12,790
How can you so adamantly believe

203
00:28:12,790 --> 00:28:16,610
that your texts can't just be ignored?

204
00:28:16,610 --> 00:28:20,790
What religion is it that you're believing with all your might?

205
00:28:20,790 --> 00:28:24,440
Are you giving your tithes on time?

206
00:28:36,220 --> 00:28:42,250
Are you ignoring my messages?

207
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:51,220
Sis, how could he really do something like that?

208
00:28:51,220 --> 00:28:55,670
If I sent 11 messages, shouldn't he reply to at least 1?

209
00:28:55,670 --> 00:29:00,220
It can't be that he doesn't know Hangul (Korean Alphabet). Are the messages being swallowed?

210
00:29:00,220 --> 00:29:02,660
Hey.

211
00:29:02,660 --> 00:29:07,270
You easily send me more than 10 useless texts a day.

212
00:29:07,270 --> 00:29:09,680
Did you see me responding?

213
00:29:10,850 --> 00:29:13,070
Did you not know I didn't reply?

214
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:20,370
That's... because I see you all the time. At home, and at school...

215
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:24,880
Let's not talk.

216
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:27,130
Let's go together, Unni.

217
00:29:29,390 --> 00:29:31,820
What are you doing?

218
00:29:33,730 --> 00:29:35,760
It's Dong Soo.

219
00:29:42,840 --> 00:29:46,390
Unni! Unni!

220
00:29:47,070 --> 00:29:50,390
-Are you Dong Soo?
-Yeah.

221
00:29:52,250 --> 00:29:54,150
You know her right?

222
00:29:56,730 --> 00:29:58,150
Yeah.

223
00:29:58,150 --> 00:30:00,980
-Why do you ignore her messages?
-Huh?

224
00:30:00,980 --> 00:30:06,540
I find her whining really annoying. Whether you reply to her messages,

225
00:30:06,540 --> 00:30:12,640
or if you tell her confidently that you don't like her, just muffle her. Understood?

226
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:24,200
♫ Even if you don't love me, I can give myself to you. ♫

227
00:30:24,200 --> 00:30:29,800
♫ You, my love, that I've waited for so long. ♫

228
00:30:29,800 --> 00:30:35,400
♫ Don't hesitate. The path we go down ♫

229
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:40,510
♫ will only be full of happiness. ♫

230
00:30:40,510 --> 00:30:46,910
♫ All the times that were lonely, ♫

231
00:30:46,910 --> 00:30:48,790
Right, today's lesson is over.

232
00:30:48,790 --> 00:30:57,090
Thank you!

233
00:30:57,090 --> 00:31:00,940
Huh?

234
00:31:00,940 --> 00:31:03,470
Huh? It's Dong Soo.

235
00:31:03,470 --> 00:31:08,350
♫ So that I can express my feelings to you. ♫

236
00:31:08,350 --> 00:31:15,470
♫ I'll be there 1, I'll be there two. I'll only love you. ♫

237
00:31:15,470 --> 00:31:22,380
♫ If I'm with you,  ♫

238
00:31:23,670 --> 00:31:26,730
Hyo Seon's here.

239
00:31:30,060 --> 00:31:34,020
Why? Why did you come crying, why?

240
00:31:38,810 --> 00:31:43,490
I got a message from Dong Soo.

241
00:31:45,230 --> 00:31:46,880
I'm back.

242
00:31:46,880 --> 00:31:48,590
You came?

243
00:31:49,830 --> 00:31:53,920
Unni, thank you.

244
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:58,580
Thanks to you, I got a message from Dong Soo.

245
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:12,770
A response came saying to never message him again.

246
00:32:12,770 --> 00:32:18,940
Don't cry, my child. It's okay, it's okay.

247
00:32:18,940 --> 00:32:25,260
Don't cry, don't cry.

248
00:32:25,260 --> 00:32:32,200
Oh gosh, don't cry. My world, don't cry.

249
00:32:56,170 --> 00:32:58,020
Are you studying?

250
00:32:58,780 --> 00:33:00,910
Can you come out for a moment?

251
00:33:21,430 --> 00:33:23,350
I'm fine.

252
00:33:27,540 --> 00:33:29,260
Today...

253
